  // on it: the strip's own pixels say where its values are (connected-component
  // row bands), and EVERY band inside the data corridor gets its own tight-crop
  // OCR (binarised + upscaled, psm 7, psm 13 retry). dataRows is used only as a
  // vertical CORRIDOR (skip the header above the first shot and the AVERAGE /
  // STD DEV summary rows below the last) — never as slots. Rows are then lined
  // up across strips purely by the y-position of the reads themselves: when the
  // counts match they align 1:1; a strip that misses one leaves a blank at that
  // spot and nothing shifts.
